---
---

<section
  id="quickstart"
  class="py-16 sm:py-20 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-7xl mx-auto border-t-2 border-ink/15"
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight uppercase leading-none">
      Quickstart{' '}
      <span class="font-serif italic font-normal normal-case text-[#FF4F18]">in Go.</span>
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-lg sm:text-xl text-ink/80 font-medium">
      Use OmniBuf directly on your existing <code>.pb.go</code> structs with zero codegen, or add{' '}
      <code>protoc-gen-omnibuf</code> to your <code>buf.gen.yaml</code> for generated single-pass
      methods and lazy <code>Opaque</code> wire splicing.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="border-t-2 border-ink divide-y-2 divide-ink/20">
    <!-- Row 1: Drop-in Table Engine (No Codegen Required) -->
    <div class="py-8 sm:py-10 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-8 items-center">
      <div class="lg:col-span-5 space-y-3">
        <div class="inline-block font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase px-2.5 py-1 bg-[#FAF8F2] border border-ink rounded">
          Option 1: Zero Codegen
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight leading-snug">
          Drop-in on existing <code>.pb.go</code> structs
        </h3>
        <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-ink/85 leading-relaxed max-w-[65ch]">
          OmniBuf inspects your existing <code>.pb.go</code> structs once per type, caches an unsafe
          pointer-offset table, and encodes or decodes packets without needing an extra code
          generation step.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-7 min-w-0">
        <div class="p-4 sm:p-5 bg-ink text-paper rounded-md font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm overflow-x-auto leading-relaxed border-2 border-ink">
          <div>
            <span class="text-paper/60 select-none">$ </span>go get github.com/sudorandom/omnibuf
          </div>
          <div class="mt-3 text-paper/65">// Encode any existing *pb.PeerUpdate struct:</div>
          <div>
            pkt, err := <span class="text-acid font-bold">omnibuf.Marshal</span>(msg)
          </div>
          <div class="mt-3 text-paper/65">// Decode back into *pb.PeerUpdate:</div>
          <div>
            <span class="text-[#FF4F18] font-bold">var</span> out pb.PeerUpdate
          </div>
          <div>
            err = <span class="text-acid font-bold">omnibuf.Unmarshal</span>(pkt, &amp;out)
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Row 2: Buf Code Generation -->
    <div class="py-8 sm:py-10 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-8 items-center">
      <div class="lg:col-span-5 space-y-3">
        <div class="inline-block font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase px-2.5 py-1 bg-acid border border-ink rounded">
          Option 2: Buf Plugin (Fastest)
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight leading-snug">
          Use the OmniBuf plugin for maximum performance
        </h3>
        <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-ink/85 leading-relaxed max-w-[65ch]">
          Add <code>protoc-gen-omnibuf</code> to your <code>buf.gen.yaml</code> and run{' '}
          <code>buf generate</code> to emit zero-allocation single-pass <code>MarshalOmniBuf</code>{' '}
          and <code>UnmarshalOmniBuf</code> methods directly on your generated structs.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-7 space-y-3.5 min-w-0">
        <div class="p-4 sm:p-5 bg-[#FAF8F2] text-ink rounded-md font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm overflow-x-auto leading-relaxed border-2 border-ink">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase text-ink/70 mb-1.5">buf.gen.yaml</div>
          <pre class="leading-snug">version: v2
plugins:
  - local: protoc-gen-go
    out: gen
    opt: paths=source_relative
  - local: <span class="text-[#FF4F18] font-bold">protoc-gen-omnibuf</span>
    out: gen
    opt: paths=source_relative</pre>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 sm:p-5 bg-ink text-paper rounded-md font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm overflow-x-auto leading-relaxed border-2 border-ink">
          <div>
            <span class="text-paper/60 select-none">$ </span>go install
            github.com/sudorandom/omnibuf/cmd/protoc-gen-omnibuf@latest
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="text-paper/60 select-none">$ </span>
            <span class="text-acid font-bold">buf generate</span>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-3 text-paper/65">
            // Encode *pb.PeerUpdate with generated single-pass method:
          </div>
          <div>
            pkt := msg.<span class="text-acid font-bold">MarshalOmniBufAppend</span>(nil)
          </div>
          <div class="mt-3 text-paper/65">// Decode back into *pb.PeerUpdate:</div>
          <div>
            <span class="text-[#FF4F18] font-bold">var</span> out pb.PeerUpdate
          </div>
          <div>
            err := out.<span class="text-acid font-bold">UnmarshalOmniBuf</span>(pkt, false)
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
